  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a4e42b643dc86b74e95b433dd3290285, type: 3}
  m_Name: EpitaphDatabase
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::EpitaphDatabase
  epitaphs:
  - "Here rests Elara Voss, who took the sea's storms and gave them back as songs."
  - "Captain Aurelius Brand — he sailed past the horizon and found no enemy there,
    only stars."
  - "Mirella von Hagen, healer of three villages. Death came for her as a friend,
    never as a victor."
  - "Beneath this stone sleeps Jorun the Silent, who spoke with trees — and the
    forest listens still."
  - "Isolde Fenn — she caught the lightning in glass and gave a hundred homes
    their light."
  - "Here lies Theobald Grau, clockmaker. His last clock stopped the moment his heart
    did."
  - "Seraphina Nacht, wanderer between worlds. She went on ahead, to learn the way."
  - "General Corvin Aschenfeld — a thousand battles, one promise kept: he died
    with empty hands and a clear conscience."
  - "Here rests Ottilie Morgenstern, who counted every sunrise. They came to 29,517."
  - "Balthasar Kr\xE4he, cartographer of the unknown. This last border he could not
    chart himself."
  - "Lysandra Thorn — a queen without a crown, a mother without borders, a legend
    without end."
  - "Emmerich Halm, the bellringer. Sixty years he called the living; now the bells
    ring for him."
  - "Here sleeps Rosalind Ferner, who wrote a thousand letters and not one farewell."
  - "Magnus Eichwald, smith of the seven bridges. What he joined together outlasts
    his name."
  - "Cassia Windrose — she danced against every storm, and lost to only this
    one."
  - "Here rests Alarich Nebelgang, warden of the north gate. None ever passed him,
    until sleep did."
